      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was quite the exercise in frustration :)\n\nThe decision tree looks something like\n\n-- Sequoia only supports Xcode \u003e\u003d 16\n\n-- our clang15 toolchain blows up scpectacularly when trying to compile objc with XC16 frameworks:\n\n```\nIn file included from tools/window/MetalWindowContext.mm:8:\nIn file included from ./tools/window/MetalWindowContext.h:17:\nIn file included from external/clang_mac/symlinks/xcode/MacSDK/System/Library/Frameworks/Metal.framework/Headers/Metal.h:9:\nIn file included from external/clang_mac/symlinks/xcode/MacSDK/System/Library/Frameworks/Metal.framework/Headers/MTLTypes.h:8:\nIn file included from external/clang_mac/symlinks/xcode/MacSDK/System/Library/Frameworks/Foundation.framework/Headers/Foundation.h:9:\nexternal/clang_mac/symlinks/xcode/MacSDK/System/Library/Frameworks/Foundation.framework/Headers/NSObjCRuntime.h:626:74: error: unknown type name \u0027NSUInteger\u0027\nFOUNDATION_EXPORT const char *NSGetSizeAndAlignment(const char *typePtr, NSUInteger * _Nullable sizep, NSUInteger * _Nullable alignp);\n                                                                         ^\nexternal/clang_mac/symlinks/xcode/MacSDK/System/Library/Frameworks/Foundation.framework/Headers/NSObjCRuntime.h:626:104: error: unknown type name \u0027NSUInteger\u0027\nFOUNDATION_EXPORT const char *NSGetSizeAndAlignment(const char *typePtr, NSUInteger * _Nullable sizep, NSUInteger * _Nullable alignp);\n...\n...\n```\n(I looked into it and it seems that some of the builtin macros are borked and they mess up `TARGET_OS_OSX` detection in XC\u0027s `TargetConditionals.h`)\n\n-- latest llvm releases (19.x) no longer publish any mac binaries\n\n-- *some* llvm 18 releases have arm64-apple binaries, but they seem to have issues (complaining about missing `default` branches in exhaustive `switch` statements)\n\n-- last llvm 17 (17.0.6) does have arm64-apple binaries and appears to work\n\n-- no x86_64-apple binaries released beyond llvm 15\n\nKinda sucks to have different toolchain versions for intel vs arm, we should figure out a way forward for Intel.  But I don\u0027t think we\u0027re making anything worse, afaict bazel builds are all broken on recent macs.",
